'''''Arruazu''''' '''(DDH/CVM-83)''' is an [[W:Amphibious assault ship|amphibious assault ship]] of the Baliscan [[Confederal Navy]] (''Marina confederales''). Officially an [[W:Aircraft carrier|aircraft-carrying]] multi-role [[W:Cruiser|cruiser]], and previously classified as a multi-purpose operation [[W:Destroyer|destroyer]], ''Arruazu'' is the [[W:Lead ship|lead ship]] of it's class, and was followed by the ''[[BB Talcahuano (DDH-84)|BB Talcahuano]]'' in 2017. In line with the [[Naval Vessels Naming Initiative]], ''Arruazu's'' namesake is a mountain peak in the [[Cadaqués]] region ([[Cerdanya]]).

''Arruazu'' has made three deployments to the [[Shendan Ocean|Shendan]] and [[Kendryian Ocean|Kendryian]] oceans between 2015 and 2017 while based at [[Naval Station Arayamar]]. In June 2017, the ''Arruazu'' was selected by the Confederal Naval Command as the flagship of [[Expeditionary Strike Force 3]], the first forward-based Baliscan carrier strike group, home-ported at [[Joint Base Ajowa]] in [[Sanyan]] as part of the [[Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement|Mutual Defense Initiative]] of the [[Concepción Organization of Cooperation]].

